  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "callout",
      "kind": "tip",
      "title": "After this PDF you can",
      "bullets": [
        "recognise and use the main values of se",
        "choose between passive with ser, se passive and impersonal se (and agreement)",
        "nominalise: turn verbs into nouns for a formal register",
        "use light-verb collocations (llevar a cabo, dar lugar a, hacer hincapié en)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "h1",
      "text": "1. The values of se"
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "style": "plain",
      "widths": [
        4.2,
        6.4,
        6.4
      ],
      "head": [
        "Value",
        "Example",
        "English"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Reflexive",
          "Juan se lava.",
          "Juan washes himself."
        ],
        [
          "Reciprocal",
          "Se abrazaron.",
          "They hugged each other."
        ],
        [
          "Pronominal verb",
          "Se arrepiente. Se queja.",
          "He regrets. He complains."
        ],
        [
          "Passive reflexive",
          "Se venden pisos.",
          "Flats are sold."
        ],
        [
          "Impersonal",
          "Se vive bien aquí.",
          "One lives well here."
        ],
        [
          "Accidental",
          "Se me cayó el vaso.",
          "I dropped the glass."
        ],
        [
          "Replaces le / les",
          "Se lo di.",
          "I gave it to him."
        ],
        [
          "Intensive (ethical dative)",
          "Se comió todo. Se leyó el libro.",
          "He ate it all up. He read the whole book."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "h1",
      "text": "2. Passive reflexive vs impersonal se"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "With a <b>thing</b> as the real subject, the verb agrees with it. With a <b>person as direct object</b>, the personal <b>a</b> appears and the verb stays <b>singular</b> (impersonal)."
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "style": "plain",
      "widths": [
        5.6,
        5.6,
        5.8
      ],
      "head": [
        "Passive reflexive (agrees)",
        "Impersonal se + a (singular)",
        "Note"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Se buscan secretarios.",
          "Se busca a los secretarios.",
          "indefinite vs specific"
        ],
        [
          "Se ven casas desde aquí.",
          "Se ve a los niños jugar.",
          "thing vs person"
        ],
        [
          "Se necesitan voluntarios.",
          "Se necesita a Pedro.",
          "indefinite vs specific person"
        ],
        [
          "Se oyen ruidos.",
          "Se oye a los vecinos.",
          "thing vs person"
        ],
        [
          "Se venden coches.",
          "Se detuvo a los sospechosos.",
          "thing vs person"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "bullets",
      "items": [
        "<b>Se + infinitive or subordinate clause</b>: <i>Se prohíbe fumar. Se dice que va a llover. Se cree que ha muerto.</i> (always singular)",
        "<b>Se + verb + que</b> for reports: <i>Se espera que ... / Se calcula que ... / Se estima que ... / Se prevé que ...</i>",
        "<b>Estructura de uno</b>: <i>Uno nunca sabe.</i> <i>Una no puede hacerlo todo.</i>"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "callout",
      "kind": "warn",
      "title": "Avoid ambiguity",
      "text": "<b>Se lava a los niños</b> can read as reflexive or impersonal. Write <i>Los niños se lavan</i> (they wash themselves) or <i>Se lava a los niños</i> (someone washes the children). Use the passive with ser for clarity when needed."
    },
    {
      "type": "h1",
      "text": "3. Passive voice in formal writing"
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "style": "plain",
      "widths": [
        5.0,
        6.2,
        5.8
      ],
      "head": [
        "Structure",
        "Example",
        "English"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "ser + participle + por",
          "La ley fue aprobada por el Congreso.",
          "The law was passed by Congress."
        ],
        [
          "se + verb (no agent)",
          "Se aprobó la ley.",
          "The law was passed."
        ],
        [
          "estar + participle (result)",
          "La ley está aprobada.",
          "The law is passed."
        ],
        [
          "quedar + participle",
          "Quedó aprobada la ley.",
          "The law was left approved."
        ],
        [
          "resultar + participle",
          "Resultaron heridas tres personas.",
          "Three people were injured."
        ],
        [
          "verse + participle",
          "Se vio obligado a dimitir.",
          "He was forced to resign."
        ],
        [
          "llevarse a cabo (se)",
          "Se llevó a cabo la reunión.",
          "The meeting was held."
        ],
        [
          "es de + inf.",
          "Es de esperar que mejore.",
          "It is to be expected that it improves."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "callout",
      "kind": "tip",
      "title": "Agent or no agent?",
      "text": "If you name the doer, use <b>ser + participle + por</b>. If the doer is unknown or unimportant, use <b>se</b>. Both avoid saying \"someone\"."
    },
    {
      "type": "h1",
      "text": "4. Nominalisation"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Formal writing prefers <b>nouns</b> to verb clauses. Convert verbs into nouns to make sentences compact and impersonal."
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "style": "plain",
      "widths": [
        6.4,
        6.4,
        4.2
      ],
      "head": [
        "Verb clause (spoken)",
        "Noun phrase (written)",
        "Suffix"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Cuando se aprobó la ley, ...",
          "Tras la aprobación de la ley, ...",
          "-ción"
        ],
        [
          "Porque subieron los precios, ...",
          "Debido a la subida de los precios, ...",
          "-ida"
        ],
        [
          "Si se aplica esta medida, ...",
          "De aplicarse esta medida / Con la aplicación de ...",
          "-ción"
        ],
        [
          "Al crecer la economía, ...",
          "Con el crecimiento de la economía, ...",
          "-miento"
        ],
        [
          "Aunque aumenten las ventas, ...",
          "A pesar del aumento de las ventas, ...",
          "-o"
        ],
        [
          "Después de que se firmó el acuerdo, ...",
          "Tras la firma del acuerdo, ...",
          "-a"
        ],
        [
          "Para que mejore la situación, ...",
          "Para la mejora de la situación, ...",
          "-a"
        ],
        [
          "Que se pueda ahorrar es importante.",
          "El ahorro es importante. / La posibilidad de ahorrar ...",
          "-o"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "bullets",
      "items": [
        "<b>Useful frames:</b> <i>el hecho de que, la posibilidad de que, la necesidad de, la existencia de, la ausencia de, la falta de, la tendencia a, la capacidad de</i>.",
        "<b>Too many nouns</b> can sound heavy. Mix nominal and verbal style in your own writing."
      ]
    },
